> I don't often have to write frontend code, but when I do, there is very little in terms of interactivity you cannot do with HTML these days, worst case a little sprinkle of something like HTMX.And for some front-end form field validation in the spirit of htmx, ParsleyJS[0] is quite nice. Below is one way to enable the former to support the latter:  htmx.defineExtension (
      'parsley-validation',
      {
          onEvent : function (name, evt) {
              var allow = true;

              if (name === 'htmx:load')
                  $(evt.target).parsley ();
              else if (name === 'htmx:confirm') {
                  var theForm = $(evt.target).parsley ();

                  theForm.validationResult = allow = theForm.isValid ();

                  if (!allow)
                      evt.preventDefault ();
              }

              return allow;
          }
      }
  )

